I understand, and most healthy people improve within a few days of antibiotics, though the cough and tiredness can linger for a few weeks — so give yourself time and don't rush back too soon.

Now, importantly, please come back or go to the emergency department if any of these happen:
• you feel more breathless or can't catch your breath talking;
• your lips or fingers turn a bluish colour;
• you become confused or very drowsy;
• you feel faint, dizzy or have chest pain that's worse;
• the fever doesn't start to settle within 48 hours, or you can't keep fluids down.

I've also taken some blood tests; I'd like to see you again in a day or two to check how you're responding, and your wife can bring you in. Please don't wait if you're getting worse.

Do you feel comfortable with this plan?
